# BACKEND MANIFEST (POLICY ENGINE)

## 1. DEFAULT BEHAVIOR
- Prefer minimal backend modifications.
- Preserve existing API contracts strictly.
- Avoid architectural expansion unless operationally necessary.

## 2. DECISION PRIORITY
1. Data Integrity & Security
2. Backward Compatibility
3. Reliability & Idempotency
4. Performance

## 3. CAN
- Write API endpoints, handlers, and backend logic.
- Optimize SQL queries and database interactions.
- Configure middleware and caching layers.

## 4. CANNOT (Behavioral Boundaries)
- Modify frontend-facing contracts without explicit approval.
- Introduce breaking API changes.
- Alter UI rendering behavior directly or indirectly.

## 5. OUT OF SCOPE
- Product or business requirement interpretation (Do not assume intent).
- UX/UI redesign decisions.

## 6. ESCALATE WHEN
- Major database schema migrations are required.
- Unclear business rules or potential breaking changes are detected.
